t from its loss of patent exclusivity on Humira. Novo Nordisk maintains a dominant lead in the rapidly expanding metabolic...\n\n11 days ago - The Motley Fool\n\n### Top Analyst Reports for Walmart, Visa & Novo Nordisk\n\nWalmart, Visa and Novo Nordisk headline today's analyst reports, with digital growth, payment innovation and obesity-drug demand offset by rising costs and competition.\n\n### GLP-1 Drugs May Slow Aging By Upto Four Years, Early Research Suggest\n\n(RTTNews) - New research from Novo Nordisk A/S (NVO) and Eli Lilly and Company (LLY) suggests that their GLP-1 drugs may slow down certain biological signs of aging by two to four years.\n\n### Novo Nordisk price target lowered to $40 from $47 at BMO Capital","title":"Novo Nordisk (NVO) Stock Price & Overview","url":"https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/nvo/"},{"author":null,"id":"https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/nvo/statistics/","image":"https://stockanalysis.com/stockanalysis-1200x630.png","text":"Novo Nordisk (NVO) Statistics & Valuation\n\n39.05 -0.38 (-0.96%) At close: Oct 23, 2026, 4:00 PM EDT\n\n39.03 -0.02 (-0.05%) After-hours: Oct 23, 2026, 7:59 PM EDT\n\n## Total Valuation\n\nNovo Nordisk has a market cap or net worth of $172.38 billion. The enterprise value is $186.63 billion.\n\n| Market Cap | 172.38B |\n| --- | --- |\n| Enterprise Value | 186.63B |\n\n## Important Dates\n\nThe next confirmed earnings date is Wednesday, November 4, 2026, before market open.\n\n| Earnings Date | Nov 4, 2026 |\n| --- | --- |\n| Ex-Dividend Date | Aug 17, 2026 |\n\n## Share Statistics\n\nNovo Nordisk has 4.43 billion shares outstanding. The number of shares has decreased by -0.14% in one year.\n\n| Current Share Class | n/a |\n| --- | --- |\n| Shares Outstanding | 4.43B |\n| Shares Change (YoY) | -0.14% |\n| Shares Change (QoQ) | -0.29% |\n| Owned by Insiders (%) | 0.02% |\n| Owned by Institutions (%) | 27.56% |\n| Float | 3.17B |\n\n## Valuation Ratios\n\nThe trailing PE ratio is 9.93 and the forward PE ratio is 11