nings were $2.67 billion, an increase of 7.52%.\n\n## Analyst Summary\n\nAccording to 17 analysts, the average rating for ZTS stock is \"Buy.\" The 12-month stock price target is $93.0, which is an increase of 14.77% from the latest price.\n\nPrice Target $93.0 (14.77% upside) Analyst Consensus: Buy\n\n### Zoetis Transcript: Morgan Stanley 24th Annual Global Healthcare Conference\n\n### Zoetis confirms FDA Emergency Use Authorization for Simparica Trio\n\nZoetis (ZTS) announced that Simparica Trio has received Emergency Use Authorization from the U.S. FDA for the treatment of infestations caused by New World screwworm larvae in dogs and puppies.\n\n2 months ago - TheFly\n\n### Zoetis Receives Emergency Use Authorization for Simparica Trio® (sarolaner, moxidectin, and pyrantel chewable tablets) for Treatment of New World Screwworm Infestations in Dogs and Puppies\n\nPARSIPPANY, N.J.--(BUSINESS WIRE)---- $ZTS #animalhealth--Zoetis Inc. today announced that Simparica Trio has received Emergency Use Authorization (EUA) from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA...\n\n2 months ago - Business Wire\n\n### Zoetis gets US FDA emergency use nod for treatment for screwworm in dogs\n\nThe U.S. Food and Drug Administration on Thursday issued an emergency use authorization for Zoetis' flea and ​tick drug to treat New World screwworm (NWS) infestations ‌in dogs and puppies.\n\n2 months ago - Reuters\n\n### Zoetis price target lowered to $96 from $112 at Citi\n\nCiti lowered the firm’s price target on Zoetis (ZTS) to $96 from $112 and keeps a Buy rating on the shares. The firm updated its ratings and targets in the…\n\n2 months ago - TheFly\n\n### Zoetis price target lowered to $80 from $90 at Piper Sandler\n\nPiper Sandler analyst David Westenberg lowered the firm’s price target on Zoetis (ZTS) to $80 from $90 and keeps a Neutral rating on the shares following quarterly results. The firm…\n\n2 months ago - TheFly\n\n### Zoetis price target lowered to $85 from $99 at Morgan Stanley\n\nMorgan Stanley lowered the firm’s price target on Zoetis (ZTS) to $85 from $99 and keeps an Overweight rating on the shares.\n\n### Zoetis price target lowered to $80 from $85 at UBS\n\nUBS analyst Andrea Alfonso lowered the firm’s price target on Zoetis (ZTS) to $80 from $85 and keeps a Neutral rating on the shares.\n\n### Zoetis Earnings Call Transcript: Q2 2026\n\nQ2 2026 saw flat revenue and a 2% decline in adjusted net income, with U.S. companion animal under pressure from declining clinic visits and heightened competition, while international and livestock segments showed growth. Full-year guidance was revised downward, reflecting persistent headwinds and increased promotional activity.\n\n2 months ago - Transcripts","title":"Zoetis (ZTS) Stock Price & Overview","url":"https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/zts/"},{"author":null,"id":"https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/zts/statistics/","image":"https://stockanalysis.com/stockanalysis-1200x630.png","text":"Zoetis (ZTS) Statistics & Valuation\n\n81.03 -0.97 (-1.18%) At close: Oct 23, 2026, 4:00 PM EDT\n\n80.08 -0.95 (-1.18%) After-hours: Oct 23, 2026, 7:49 PM EDT\n\n## Total Valuation\n\nZoetis has a market cap or net worth of $33.48 billion. The enterprise value is $41.06 billion.\n\n| Market Cap | 33.48B |\n| --- | --- |\n| Enterprise Value | 41.06B |\n\n## Important Dates\n\nThe next confirmed earnings date is Thursday, November 5, 2026, before market open.\n\n| Earnings Date | Nov 5, 2026 |\n| --- | --- |\n| Ex-Dividend Date | Oct 30, 2026 |\n\n## Share Statistics\n\nZoetis has 413.22 million shares outstanding. The number of shares has decreased by -4.22% in one year.\n\n| Current Share Class | 413.22M |\n| --- | --- |\n| Shares Outstanding | 413.22M |\n| Shares Change (YoY) | -4.22% |\n| Shares Change (QoQ) | -1.11% |\n| Owned by Insiders (%) | 0.10% |\n| Owned by Institutions (%) | 98.43% |\n| Float | 412.37M |\n\n## Valuation Ratios\n\nThe trailing PE ratio is 13.22 and the forward PE ratio is 13.12. Zo